<title>USA: FSA qualifies nine muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies nine muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Wednesday it qualified for bond insurance the following nine municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Elgin, Ill., $21.64 million general obligation bonds.  </p>
<p>--Florida Board of Education, $17.5 million bonds.</p>
<p>--Newburyport, Mass., $5.02 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Livingston County, Mich., $2.975 million water bonds.</p>
<p>--Clifton Board of Education, N.J., $15.3 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Poughkeepsie, N.Y., $6.425 million public improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Pittsburgh, Pa., $37.38 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Montgomery Municipal Utility District No 40, Texas, $2.55 million unlimited tax bonds.</p>
<p>--Montgomery Municipal Utility District No 7, Texas, $1.19 million bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
